    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "Clinical picture (stiffness, cramps, dystonic posturing); EMG showing continuous motor activity with normal morphology, more prominent in the paraspinal muscles, decreasing after midazolam; strongly positive anti-amphiphysin antibodies",
      "quote": "SPS was the likely diagnosis based on the clinical picture. An electromyography (EMG) study was carried out, which showed continuous motor activity with normal morphology, more prominent in the paraspinal muscles, and after administering 2 mg midazolam, the activity decreased significantly and was absent for a brief period. This finding was consistent with a diagnosis of SPS. A neuronal antibody profile test was done, which was strongly positive for anti-amphiphysin antibodies.",
